---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { rel, SUPPORT_EMAIL, LEGAL_NAME } from '../../consts';
const description = `Privacy policy for Beat the Dealer: Card Counting by ${LEGAL_NAME}.`;
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy · Beat the Dealer: Card Counting" description={description} path="/privacy/beat-the-dealer">
  <main class="page">
    <div class="wrap" style="max-width:720px;">
      <a class="back" href={rel('/privacy/')}>← All privacy policies</a>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Beat the Dealer: Card Counting · Effective date: September 7, 2026</p>

      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        {LEGAL_NAME} operates Beat the Dealer, a free offline blackjack trainer for adults 18+ supported
        by ads. There are no accounts, and your lessons, drills, progress, and settings stay on your
        device. If you choose to turn it on in Settings, Beat the Dealer can send
        <strong>anonymous usage analytics</strong> (PostHog). When a crash-reporting project is configured
        for a release build, it can also send <strong>anonymous crash reports</strong> (Sentry). Neither
        is linked to your identity or used to track you, and neither is used for advertising.
      </p>

      <h2>What stays on your device</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Your lesson and drill progress.</li>
        <li>Your app settings, including purchase/ads state and optional analytics consent.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This information is stored locally on your device. We do not receive lesson content, answers,
        cards, counts, or free text you see in the app. Deleting the app removes local app data from
        your device.
      </p>

      <h2>Usage analytics (PostHog) — off by default, Settings opt-in</h2>
      <p>
        Optional first-party product analytics can measure orientation and supported lesson or drill
        completion, plus coarse ad-funnel steps. Events contain no cards, answers, or free text. Events
        are tied to a random ID generated on your device after you opt in, not to your name or any
        account (Beat the Dealer has no accounts). Analytics stays off until you tap
        <strong>Enable Optional Analytics</strong> in Settings.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Disable and Delete Analytics</strong> in Settings stops new events, clears the local
          send queue, and requests deletion of already-sent events for that install ID.
        </li>
        <li>
          Events already sent are kept for <strong>90 days</strong> as individual records and up to
          <strong>13 months</strong> as aggregated statistics.
        </li>
        <li>
          If you need help with a deletion request, copy the analytics ID shown in Settings (before you
          turn analytics off, since switching off resets the ID) and email
          <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Crash reporting (Sentry)</h2>
      <p>
        When crash reporting is configured for a release build, a crash can send an anonymous report —
        the stack trace and your iOS version — so we can find and fix the problem. A crash report never
        contains cards, answers, progress detail, or anything else from your lessons. Crash reports are
        kept for <strong>30 days</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising (Google AdMob)</h2>
      <p>
        The free version may show interstitial ads between sessions. Ads are served by
        <strong>Google AdMob</strong>, a third-party advertising network. Beat the Dealer requests
        <strong>non-personalized</strong> ads and does not show Apple's tracking prompt, because it does
        not ask for cross-app tracking. Ads are not shown in the EU, EEA, UK, or Switzerland. To serve
        and measure ads, Google may still collect device information such as a device identifier, IP
        address, and coarse ad-interaction data. We do not receive, store, or link any of this to you,
        and it is never joined with the analytics described above.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          How Google uses this data is described in
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads">Google's advertising policy</a> and
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's privacy policy</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          A one-time Remove Ads purchase (price shown in the app) removes those interstitial ads for
          the life of the app on your device and restores across devices signed in to the same Apple ID.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Used to track you</h2>
      <p>
        None of the data described on this page is used to track you across other companies' apps or
        websites, and none of it is combined with data from a data broker. This is true for analytics,
        crash reports, and advertising alike.
      </p>

      <h2>Children and age</h2>
      <p>
        Beat the Dealer is for adults 18 and older. We do not knowingly collect any data from anyone
        under 13. There are no accounts, profiles, or in-app messaging.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy ever changes materially, the new version will be posted at this URL with an updated
        date above. Continued use of the app after a change constitutes acceptance.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions? Email <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
